From: Research Team <research@example.local>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0001/0003] RFC: mm: add MADV_SEMANTIC_* definitions to UAPI

// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
/* RFC ONLY – NOT FOR SUBMISSION */

This patch adds experimental semantic memory hints to the madvise UAPI.
These hints are designed to allow userspace to signal memory intent
(streaming vs reuse vs ephemeral) for AI inference workloads.

At this stage, no behavior is guaranteed by the kernel.

Signed-off-by: Research Team <research@example.local>
---
 include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h b/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h
index 6ce1f1ce4c0e..8b28f802d2c1 100644
--- a/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h
+++ b/include/uapi/asm-generic/mman-common.h
@@ -79,6 +79,12 @@
 
 #define MADV_COLLAPSE	25		/* Synchronous hugepage collapse */
 
+/* RFC: Semantic memory hints for inference workloads */
+#define MADV_SEMANTIC_STREAMING  30	/* Large read-once sequential access */
+#define MADV_SEMANTIC_REUSE      31	/* High-frequency random access reuse */
+#define MADV_SEMANTIC_EPHEMERAL  32	/* Temporary/short-lived allocation */
+/* End RFC */
+
 /* compatibility flags */
 #define MAP_FILE	0
 
